The `ZipFile` class contains two relevant methods for our investigation:
1. `getEntry(String name)`: This method retrieves a `ZipArchiveEntry` based on the entry name.
   ```java
   public ZipArchiveEntry getEntry(String name) {
       return nameMap.get(name);
   }
   ```

2. `getInputStream(ZipArchiveEntry ze)`: This method returns an `InputStream` for a given `ZipArchiveEntry` by creating a `BoundedInputStream` based on the data offset and compressed size of the entry.
   ```java
    public InputStream getInputStream(ZipArchiveEntry ze) throws IOException, ZipException {
        OffsetEntry offsetEntry = entries.get(ze);
        if (offsetEntry == null) {
            return null;
        }
        ZipUtil.checkRequestedFeatures(ze);
        long start = offsetEntry.dataOffset;
        BoundedInputStream bis = new BoundedInputStream(start, ze.getCompressedSize());
        switch (ze.getMethod()) {
            case ZipArchiveEntry.STORED:
                return bis;
            case ZipArchiveEntry.DEFLATED:
                bis.addDummy();
                final Inflater inflater = new Inflater(true);
                return new InflaterInputStream(bis, inflater) {
                    @Override
                    public void close() throws IOException {
                        super.close();
                        inflater.end();
                    }
                };
            default:
                throw new ZipException("Found unsupported compression method " + ze.getMethod());
        }
    }
   ```

Given the implementation of these methods, the issue might be related to how `ZipArchiveEntry` instances are associated with the correct `InputStreams`, potentially due to discrepancies in handling offsets, compressed sizes, or compression methods.

To pinpoint the exact cause, further inspection of how `ZipFile` interacts with `ZipArchiveEntry` instances during entry retrieval and stream extraction is necessary.

